{title: Jesus, Keep Me Near the Cross}
{artist: Fanny J. Crosby / William H. Doane}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response, Meditative}
{key: F}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Jesus, keep me [Bb]near the [F]cross
There a [C7]precious [F]fountain
[F]Free to all, a [Bb]healing [F]stream
[C7]Flows from Calvary's [F]mountain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
In the [F]cross, in the [Bb]cross
Be my [F]glory [C7]ever
Till my [F]raptured [Bb]soul shall [F]find
[C7]Rest be[Dm]yond the [C7]ri[F]ver
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Near the cross, a [Bb]trembling [F]soul
[C7]Love and mercy [F]found me
[F]There the Bright and [Bb]Morning [F]Star
[C7]Sheds its beams a[F]round me
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Near the cross! O [Bb]Lamb of [F]God
[C7]Bring its scenes be[F]fore me
[F]Help me walk from [Bb]day to [F]day
[C7]With its shadow o'er [F]me
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Near the cross I'll [Bb]watch and [F]wait
[C7]Hoping, trusting [F]ever
[F]Till I reach the [Bb]golden [F]strand
[C7]Just beyond the [F]river
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
